# L §2.1 Dates (tally 2.1.6, issue #48): Tally's days are 0001-01-01 to 9999-12-31, and the year 9999 and its
# quarters, months and days are whole periods; the start of the period after one that ends with 9999-12-31 is the
# end of time, which follows every day, and a duration or a day taken from it is as from any day. A run inside 9999:
# the built-in days, months and years, a month range by 3 and a year range ending 9999 load; flows over 9999, its
# December and its last day count the rents; end_of(9999-12) - 1 day is 9999-12-31, - 1 month 9999-12-01; the year
# 9999 has 365 days and its last quarter 92. Each answer is the one the same model gives in 2026 (2017..2026 for ys).
# tally 2.1.5's refcore refused the model REFCORE-NOT-YET (the days index stepped past 9999-12-31; the years index
# built 10000-01-01).
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 9999-12-31
  start 9999-01-01
  end 9999-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index flats = [f1, f2]
index qs = month 9999-01..9999-12 by 3
index ys = year 9990..9999
input rent_amt: money PLN
input rent_day[f in flats]: date
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..

def qlen[q in qs]: int = days_between(start_of(q), end_of(q))
def ylen[y in ys]: int = days_between(start_of(y), end_of(y))

move rent[f in flats]: transfers
  on rent_day[f]
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount rent_amt

version plan_9999
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 9999-01-01
  rent_amt = 2 000.00 PLN "umowa najmu"
  rent_day[f1] = 9999-06-30 "umowa najmu"
  rent_day[f2] = 9999-12-31 "umowa najmu"
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 9999-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask yd: days_between(start_of(9999), end_of(9999))
ask md: days_between(end_of(9999-12), start_of(9999-12))
ask after: 9999-12-31 < end_of(9999)
ask same: end_of(9999-12) == end_of(9999)
ask last: max(end_of(9999-12) - 1 day, 9999-06-01)
ask back: end_of(9999-12) - 1 month
ask q4: end_of(9999-Q4) - 1 day
ask qlast: qlen[9999-10]
ask ylast: ylen[9999]
ask fy: flows(konto, 9999)
ask fm: flows(konto, 9999-12)
ask fo: flows(konto, 9999-12..)
ask fd: flows(konto, 9999-12-31)
=== expect
after: true
  cut 9999-12-31
back: 9999-12-01
  cut 9999-12-31
fd: -2 000.00 PLN
  cut 9999-12-31
fm: -2 000.00 PLN
  cut 9999-12-31
fo: -2 000.00 PLN
  cut 9999-12-31
fy: -4 000.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: rent[f1]
  cut 9999-12-31
last: 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
md: -31
  cut 9999-12-31
q4: 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
qlast: 92
  cut 9999-12-31
same: true
  cut 9999-12-31
yd: 365
  cut 9999-12-31
ylast: 365
  cut 9999-12-31
